Trusted Adult Awards		 
	
		 
			

		 				
	 

	 	
 
	     


         The North Reading Community Impact Team's Youth Substance Use Prevention Coalition is seeking nominations for the 2026 Trusted Adult Award. A trusted adult is a person that a young person can go to with a problem or to talk to, typically outside of the immediate home/family. We wish to recognize individuals who are making a positive impact on the lives of our community's youth. Who can be nominated?  Any adults (18 or older) who live or work in the Town of North Reading. Organizations may not be nominated.  A nominee must be someone who is not the youth's parent, guardian nor someone who lives in the youth's home. Who can nominate?  Any youth (up to grade 12) who are citizens of the Town of North Reading. An individual may not nominate himself/herself/themself. How do I nominate someone?   Complete the Trusted Adult Award Nomination Form , and submit it to the Community Impact Team as instructed on the form, no later than Friday, May 15, 2026. How are winners selected?  Up to 5 winners will be selected by the volunteers of the Community Impact Team’s Youth Substance Use Prevention Coalition based on the nominations. What is the prize?  Winners will be presented with a 2026 Trusted Adult Award and announced in the media. Can I submit additional documents with my nomination?  Each entry may also be submitted with the following: photographs (5 max), video (no longer than 2 minutes), and/or letter of recommendation (2 max). Nomination documents and all media will not be returned and become property of the Community Impact Team. Can I nominate more than one person?  Each youth may nominate up to 2 individuals. Who can I contact with questions?  You may contact Amy Luckiewicz at  coalition@northreadingma.gov . 2026 Trusted Adult Award Nomination Form 
     

 
